    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "Reports and Insights are one destination: Overview, Insights, All reports, Yours, Shared with you, From Corelith, then Folders and Build. Explore moved out to its own place on the rail.\n\nThe builder’s outline, inspector and question shelf resize from their edges; widths are kept per person.",
     "x": 10800,
     "y": 0
    },
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "One set of pages for every workspace, shown here for Floorcode. “From Corelith” is what the app calls Built in.\n\nIn the app today: the catalogue, a report with its page, templates, export, arranging the page, built reports and Make it yours, and Management → Reports.\n\nNew in this design: the Overview, Insights for Sales and Site visits in one shape (they replace /crm/reports and /crm/insights), Send it (INS-05 and INS-09, not built), and editing a built report in the builder.",
     "x": 21440,
     "y": 1240
    },
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "/retail/reports/[ref] is the page every template row links to, and it 404s today. This is that page: the same report page in the Tender look.\n\nInsights keeps the seven retail topics as they are. Buying and Customers have no templates yet: they wait on the orders, bills, customers and accounts sources.",
     "x": 9280,
     "y": 2680
    },
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "The Fees insight replaces the Collections and Arrears tabs of /schools/reports. Remind the 41 sends a portal notice the bursar chooses to send.\n\nTeachers keep their class page in the teacher portal.",
     "x": 7760,
     "y": 4080
    },
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "The Production insight replaces /dashboard, the Production Dashboard filed under Settings. It reads shift reports as well as plant reports.\n\n/gold/insights/allocations is a work queue, so it moves to Gold → Allocations.",
     "x": 7760,
     "y": 5460
    },
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "Payroll has no reports page today. P2 and the NSSA schedule are listed under Pay and open on the returns page, whose Export buttons are not wired yet.\n\nThe workshop gets Stores and maintenance first, because the area order follows the product, not only the profile.",
     "x": 7760,
     "y": 6860
    }
   ]
